WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:08.520
So now, before we deep dive to the formatting and casting, I would like you to understand what is

00:08.520 --> 00:09.400
date formats.

00:09.440 --> 00:10.440
So back to our example.

00:10.440 --> 00:13.040
We have here the date and time informations.

00:13.040 --> 00:16.200
And we understood there is components year, month day and so on.

00:16.240 --> 00:20.400
Now if you check the date time there is combination of numbers and characters.

00:20.400 --> 00:26.520
For example the 2025 is a number, but between the month and the year there is like a minus between

00:26.520 --> 00:26.720
them.

00:26.720 --> 00:27.800
And this is a character.

00:27.800 --> 00:30.400
So now this is a very specific format.

00:30.400 --> 00:34.240
And in SQL we can have a code for this format.

00:34.240 --> 00:37.560
So for example let's start with the year we have here four digits.

00:37.560 --> 00:40.480
And we can represent it with four y.

00:40.680 --> 00:42.000
So y y y.

00:42.160 --> 00:46.160
And we call those characters as a format specifiers.

00:46.160 --> 00:48.680
So this is how we represent the year.

00:48.840 --> 00:52.200
Then between the year and the month there is like this small minus.

00:52.200 --> 00:54.160
And then the month is two digits.

00:54.160 --> 01:00.040
And we can represent it with two big m, so m then between the month and the day there is a minus.

01:00.040 --> 01:01.400
So we have as well minus.

01:01.400 --> 01:04.320
And then the day represented with two digits d.

01:05.080 --> 01:08.040
And then we have like a space between the date and time.

01:08.040 --> 01:09.320
And then we start with the date.

01:09.320 --> 01:14.040
So it starts with the hour big H and big H, because here we have the system of 24.

01:14.040 --> 01:17.240
And then we have double points small m, small m.

01:17.280 --> 01:20.320
So as you can see here, the formats are case sensitive.

01:20.480 --> 01:23.800
So there is a big difference between small M and big M.

01:23.800 --> 01:28.960
So a small M indicates for a minute and big M indicates for a month.

01:28.960 --> 01:31.960
So as you can see here the case format is case sensitive.

01:31.960 --> 01:34.440
So two small m means minutes.

01:34.440 --> 01:39.280
But two capital M means month then double point and small twos.

01:39.320 --> 01:43.000
So now the whole code is called the date format.

01:43.000 --> 01:46.560
So this is the date format representation of this value.

01:46.560 --> 01:50.640
Now in the world there are different representations on how to represent a date.

01:50.640 --> 01:56.080
So for example in SQL we have the international standard ISO 60 801.

01:56.080 --> 01:58.360
And the date format is like we have learned.

01:58.400 --> 01:59.880
First it starts with a year.

01:59.880 --> 02:05.480
So four digits for the years, minus two digits for the month minus two digit for the day.

02:05.480 --> 02:07.280
So year month day.

02:07.280 --> 02:09.720
But in the USA we have different standards.

02:09.720 --> 02:11.960
So first it starts with the month.

02:11.960 --> 02:16.050
So we have M and then after that it is followed with the day.

02:16.050 --> 02:19.810
So we have then the day and after that at the end we have the year.

02:19.810 --> 02:24.930
So this is the sentence format that is used in USA and in Europe we have different representations of

02:24.930 --> 02:25.410
the day.

02:25.450 --> 02:27.410
So it starts first with the small.

02:27.410 --> 02:30.850
So it starts with the day then the month and then the year.

02:30.850 --> 02:33.930
So this is exactly the opposite of the international standards.

02:33.930 --> 02:35.530
So as you can see we don't have one standard.

02:35.530 --> 02:38.730
We have different ways on how we represent dates.

02:38.730 --> 02:43.890
But in SQL the SQL server is following the format of the international standards.

02:43.890 --> 02:47.770
So SQL server start always with the year, then month, then day.

02:47.810 --> 02:52.650
So all dates that are used in our SQL database can be following this format.

02:56.570 --> 02:56.850
Okay.

02:56.850 --> 02:58.850
So after we understand what is date format.

02:58.890 --> 03:01.330
Now let's talk about formatting and casting.

03:01.330 --> 03:05.610
So what is formatting is changing the format of value from one to another.

03:05.610 --> 03:07.690
So we are changing how the data looks like.

03:07.690 --> 03:09.130
So for example we have our date.

03:09.130 --> 03:11.410
So it's following the international standards.

03:11.450 --> 03:13.730
Start with year month then day.

03:13.770 --> 03:19.210
Now we can go and change the format using the function format where we can go and define a different

03:19.210 --> 03:25.130
date format like it starts with the month and then we have like slash instead of minus and then the

03:25.130 --> 03:26.530
day slash year.

03:26.530 --> 03:28.090
So in the outer we're going to get it like this.

03:28.090 --> 03:30.850
And even the years is only two digits not four.

03:30.850 --> 03:34.730
So here we are providing for SQL, the format that we would like to see the data with.

03:34.770 --> 03:39.570
Or you could go with other formats where you have three big M and then four digits for the year, and

03:39.570 --> 03:41.250
between them is just a space.

03:41.250 --> 03:46.330
So in the output you will get abbreviation of the month name and then space and the year.

03:46.330 --> 03:48.530
So this is one way on how to format data.

03:48.530 --> 03:53.410
But in SQL there is another function that helps us to format data and that is convert.

03:53.410 --> 03:55.730
So here we provide not the format itself.

03:55.730 --> 03:57.570
We provide style number.

03:57.570 --> 03:59.330
So for example the style number six.

03:59.330 --> 04:01.530
So it can show it like this day space.

04:01.530 --> 04:06.650
And after that we have the abbreviation name of the month and then two digits of the year.

04:06.690 --> 04:13.050
Or if you use another style the 112, then you will get the year month day without any separation between

04:13.050 --> 04:13.370
them.

04:13.370 --> 04:17.170
And of course, not only the date and time we can style, we can style as well numbers.

04:17.170 --> 04:20.810
And here we can use the function format in order to change the format of the number.

04:20.810 --> 04:25.330
So here, if you are using the format of n numeric values, then the value is going to be separated

04:25.330 --> 04:26.130
with comma.

04:26.170 --> 04:29.940
Or if you use C for the currency, then you will get the dollar sign.

04:29.940 --> 04:32.940
Or if you go and use P then you will get the percentage.

04:32.940 --> 04:34.900
And at the end you have the percentage character.

04:34.900 --> 04:39.140
So as you can see, we can as well change the format of the numbers that only the dates.

04:39.140 --> 04:41.060
So this is what we mean by formatting.

04:41.060 --> 04:43.780
We are just changing how the value looks like.

04:43.780 --> 04:46.100
Now in the other hand the casting.

04:46.300 --> 04:50.300
The casting can go and change the data type from one to another.

04:50.300 --> 04:56.100
So for example, if we have the value one, two, three as a string, we can go and convert it from

04:56.140 --> 04:58.260
the data type string to an integer.

04:58.260 --> 05:00.540
So in the output we'll get as well 123.

05:00.540 --> 05:01.660
But as a number.

05:01.700 --> 05:05.620
Or we can go and change the data type from date to string.

05:05.620 --> 05:08.180
So in the output it is not anymore a date.

05:08.180 --> 05:10.660
It is a string value or the way around.

05:10.660 --> 05:14.340
We can change the data type from a string to a date.

05:14.340 --> 05:17.940
So as you can see, we can change the data type from one to another.

05:17.940 --> 05:20.460
And we can use that using two functions.

05:20.460 --> 05:26.980
The first one is and the most famous one is cast function or in SQL server we can use as well the convert

05:26.980 --> 05:29.660
function in order to change the data type.

05:29.660 --> 05:33.900
So this is what we mean with casting changing the data type from one to another.
